From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Biggart <swbiggart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:43:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/46] flashnext cuda: a captured decode round stages its
 inputs ahead of the capture

TF_FLASHNEXT_DECODE_GRAPH=1 at --tp 2 failed every first plain round
with UnownedCaptureSource: Cache.run set only `prepared`, so Pass.chunk
uploaded the round's token ids through the copy-source owner inside the
capture, which refuses any host source there. The round now queues its
ids, positions, lane table and n-gram rows on the stream with
stageWindow, as the one-GPU shared windows do, then captures or replays
kernels and collectives alone; an unstaged pass is refused before any
capture. A replay stages every round's inputs afresh, the lane table
included.
---
 .../families/flashnext/cuda_round_graph.zig   |  40 ++--
 .../flashnext/cuda_round_graph_test.zig       | 184 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_round_graph_test.zig

